# Motiondot — Project Rules

## Folder architecture

- **Feature-based structure**: UI and logic for a capability live under `features/<name>/` (e.g. `features/upload/components/`, `features/upload/hooks/`).
- **Shared UI only** in `components/` — never duplicate the same component in `features/` and `components/`.
- **`lib/ffmpeg/`** — all FFmpeg / fluent-ffmpeg logic. Do not call ffmpeg from `app/`, `features/`, or `worker/` directly.
- **`worker/`** — BullMQ workers and job processors only. Do not put worker runtime under `lib/workers/`.
- **`presets/`** — SNS preset definitions as **JSON files only**. Load via `features/presets/` helpers, not hardcoded in TS.

## TypeScript & styling

- **TypeScript strictly** — no new `.js` files; `strict` mode; prefer typed APIs.
- **Tailwind only** for styling — no CSS modules or inline `style={{}}` unless required for dynamic values.
- **Modular components** — small, single-purpose files.
- **`app/page.tsx`** — thin composition only (import feature views). No large JSX blocks in route files.

## Imports

- `@/features/*` — feature modules
- `@/components/*` — shared UI
- `@/lib/ffmpeg/*` — video processing
- `@/lib/storage/*` — paths and I/O
- `@/worker/*` — only from worker entry scripts, not from React components

## Anti-patterns (do not)

- Duplicate components across features
- FFmpeg calls outside `lib/ffmpeg`
- BullMQ `Worker` / `Queue` processors outside `worker/`
- Preset dimensions hardcoded in TS when a JSON exists in `presets/`
- Large `page.tsx` files or non-Tailwind styling
